2026-06-22 12:16:34,566 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-06-22 12:16:34,566 | AGENT | AIInnovation Agent answered: Our company, Faber IA, has a strong foundation in AI innovation, which is essential for creating an effective AI assistance tool for healthcare professionals. Our core approach is based on Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), where every answer is generated from passages retrieved from the client's controlled corpus, and the answer cites those passages. This grounding behavior ensures that our responses are explainable and transparent.

Our RAG capabilities include hybrid retrieval, re-ranking, query reformulation, multi-document synthesis, structured extraction, template-guided drafting, applicable rules recall during dossier handling, action and verification suggestions, and dossier-context continuity. These capabilities enable us to adapt generated content to clinical and administrative contexts, providing healthcare professionals with accurate and relevant information.

We offer two model options: a Sovereign European open-weight model (self-hosted) and top-tier proprietary models (via API). The choice between these models trades performance against explainability and sovereignty, allowing us to select the best approach per engagement. Our iterative methodology involves corpus selection and curation with the client's experts, retrieval tuning, prompt and template design per use case, and evaluation loops, ensuring that our solution meets the specific needs of healthcare professionals.

Our fine-tuning methods allow for optional fine-tuning on client material, which can further improve the performance of our models. We measure answer quality using a labeled evaluation set built with the client, focusing on groundedness, relevance, and factual support. Our performance benchmarks demonstrate the effectiveness of our approach in reducing processing and documentation times in comparable deployments.

In terms of innovation, our LLM stack and RAG capabilities enable us to provide a unique solution that combines the benefits of retrieval-augmented generation with the flexibility of fine-tuning on client-specific data. By leveraging our explainability features, such as source citations, retrieved passages, retrieval trace, and interaction logging, we can ensure transparency and trust in our recommendations or suggestions.

Overall, our AI assistance tool is designed to support healthcare professionals in their daily activities, providing them with accurate and relevant information, drafting assistance, and dossier handling support, while ensuring explainability, transparency, and compliance with regulatory requirements.
